  "question": {
    "text": "The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> Zener diode shown in the figure has negligible resistance and a knee current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math>. The minimum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>in</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> so that the voltage across it does not fall below <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"assets\\qt0058_b661b3aa8073.jpg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 164px;\" />"
  },
